{#
mail/_crypto_banner.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What a message's OpenPGP or S/MIME wrapping says, above the body.

Outside the frame for the reason every warning is (see _message_body): a lock
the mail could draw for itself would be worth nothing. Three symbols and no
more — encrypted, verified, a problem — each with one sentence; the details
(who signed, with which key) are the second line.

For an encrypted message the signature is inside the ciphertext, so the
browser fills that line in once it has decrypted (`signature` target of
mail--encrypted-message). For a signed one the server checked it in the
background (SignatureVerifier) and the state is on the row; null means the
check has not run yet.

Variables:
  message  Message, with crypto set
#}
{% set crypto = message.crypto %}
{% set state = message.signatureState ? message.signatureState.value : null %}
{% set encrypted = crypto.encrypted %}
{% set tone = encrypted or state == 'valid' ? 'secure' : (state == 'invalid' ? 'danger' : 'neutral') %}
{% set signer = message.signer ? (message.signer matches '/^[0-9a-f]+$/' ? message.signer|upper|split('', 4)|join(' ') : message.signer) : '' %}

<div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border px-3 py-2.5 mb-3
            {{ tone == 'secure' ? 'border-emerald-500/40 bg-emerald-500/10' : (tone == 'danger' ? 'border-danger/40 bg-danger/10' : 'border-line bg-raised') }}"
     data-testid="crypto-banner">
    <i class="fa-solid {{ encrypted ? 'fa-lock' : (state == 'invalid' ? 'fa-triangle-exclamation' : (state == 'valid' ? 'fa-circle-check' : 'fa-signature')) }}
              {{ tone == 'secure' ? 'text-emerald-600' : (tone == 'danger' ? 'text-danger' : 'text-ink-faint') }} mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
       aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold {{ tone == 'danger' ? 'text-danger' : 'text-ink' }}">
            {% if encrypted %}
                {{ (crypto.pgp ? 'message.crypto.encrypted' : 'message.crypto.encrypted_smime')|trans }}
            {% else %}
                {{ ('message.crypto.signed.' ~ (state ?? 'pending'))|trans }}
            {% endif %}
        </p>
        {% if encrypted %}
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted break-words" data-mail--encrypted-message-target="signature" hidden></p>
        {% elseif signer %}
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted break-words">{{ 'message.crypto.signer'|trans({ '%signer%': signer }) }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
